# Trivy vulnerability suppressions — read by the CI image scan (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml) and by `trivy image` run from the repo root.
#
# Policy: FIX vulnerabilities, don't suppress. Only add an entry when a finding
# is unfixable (no patched version) or a verified false positive, AND record a
# justification + a review date. Prefer bumping the base image or dependency.
#
# Format: one CVE / advisory ID per line, with a trailing reason comment:
#   CVE-2025-12345  # <why accepted> — review by YYYY-MM-DD
#
# (Trivy also supports an expiring .trivyignore.yaml with `expired_at:` fields
# if per-entry expiry enforcement is wanted later.)
#
# Example (commented — not active):
# CVE-2025-00000  # unfixable in node:20-alpine base; upstream tracking — review by 2026-09-01

# --- Active suppressions (none) ---
